<title>FINLAND: ESTONIA-FOREKSPANK CONSIDERS MOSCOW BRANCH.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-FOREKSPANK CONSIDERS MOSCOW BRANCH.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Estonia's Forekspank said on Tuesday that it was to open a representative office in Moscow and that it was considering opening a branch office later.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seriously considering it (opening a branch office),&quot; Forekspank chairman Ivar Lukk told Reuters at a Baltic investment conference here.  </p>
<p>Lukk said he was heading today to Moscow for the opening of the representative office and would have talks with Russian central bank officials.</p>
<p>He said that before the final decision on a branch office was made he wanted to &quot;Understand what kind of playing field will be provided.&quot;</p>
<p>--Patrick Lanninn, Helsinki +371 7 9 356 187</p>
